{"arrivo":"cs","origine":"mul-tax","origine_nome":"taxonomic name","n":6,"parole":[{"parola":"andulka","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"budgerigar","termine_origine":"Melopsittacus undulatus","catena":[{"codice":"mul-tax","nome":"taxonomic name","termine":"Melopsittacus undulatus","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"mul-tax","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Derived from taxonomic name Melopsittacus undulatus. First attested in the 20th century."},{"parola":"fejchoa","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"feijoa (Feijoa sellowiana shrub)","termine_origine":"Feijoa","catena":[{"codice":"mul-tax","nome":"taxonomic name","termine":"Feijoa","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"mul-tax","ambiti":["cucina"],"via":"","testo":"From taxonomic name Feijoa."},{"parola":"hadrosaurus","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"hadrosaur","termine_origine":"Hadrosauridae","catena":[{"codice":"mul-tax","nome":"taxonomic name","termine":"Hadrosauridae","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"ἁδρός","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Back-formation from taxonomic name Hadrosauridae, from Ancient Greek ἁδρός (hadrós, “strong”) + σαύρᾱ (saúrā, “lizard”)."},{"parola":"mechovka","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"calco","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Probably","significato":"Clitopilus (genus of fungi in the family Entolomataceae)","termine_origine":"Bryozoa","catena":[{"codice":"mul-tax","nome":"taxonomic name","termine":"Bryozoa","categoria":"calco"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"βρύον","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From mech + -ovka. * (Clitopilus): First used by Czech botanist Jan Bezděk in 1901. The name probably refers to the fact that the fungus often grows in moss (Czech mech). * (moss animal): Calque of taxonomic name Bryozoa, from Ancient Greek βρύον (brúon, “moss”) + ζῷα (zōîa), which is a plural of ζῷ"},{"parola":"ptakopysk","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"calco","incerta":"no","significato":"platypus","termine_origine":"Ornithorhynchus","catena":[{"codice":"mul-tax","nome":"taxonomic name","termine":"Ornithorhynchus","categoria":"calco"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From pták (“bird”) + -o- + pysk (“lip”). Calque of taxonomic name Ornithorhynchus, from Ancient Greek ὄρνιθ- (órnith-) (the stem of ὄρνις (órnis, “bird”)) + ῥύγχος (rhúnkhos, “snout”); Coined by Jan Svatopluk Presl (1791–1849)."},{"parola":"rhinovirus","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"rhinovirus","termine_origine":"Rhinovirus","catena":[{"codice":"mul-tax","nome":"taxonomic name","termine":"Rhinovirus","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"mul-tax","ambiti":["scienza"],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from taxonomic name Rhinovirus."}]}